window.EB_SB_ADD({"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/yX2tAtqo5zOEjJBe":{"notes":{"speed":"hover"},"abilities":[{"n":"Opportunistic Rotation","a":"r","c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The anchored dimensional would be hit by a melee or ranged Strike</p>\n<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The anchored dimensional is aware of the attack and is not Off-Guard against them</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The anchored dimensional spins their body, causing the stabilization ring to rotate into the way of the attack. The triggering Strike's damage is dealt to the stabilization ring, rather than the anchored dimensional. All other effects of the Strike affect the anchored dimensional.</p>"},{"n":"Stabilization Ring","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>An anchored dimensional is a creature from between realities forced to adopt a physical, three-dimensional form via a magitech device called a stabilization ring. The stabilization ring uses the anchored dimensional's AC and saving throws, but it has hardness 3, HP 20 (BT 10). When the stabilization ring is broken, the anchored dimensional gains concealment. When the stabilization ring is destroyed, the dimensional is freed, returning home to the incomprehensible space between realities.</p>"},{"n":"Frenetic Thrash","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The anchored dimensional lashes out in all directions, making a spined lash Strike against each adjacent enemy. Each attack counts toward their multiple attack penalty, but they don't increase their penalty until all these attacks have been made.</p>"},{"n":"Slip Through Space","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The anchored dimensional takes advantage of its tenuous relationship with space and time to outmaneuver threats. The anchored dimensional teleports to an unoccupied space they can see within 15 feet.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/6F4yHswg6zj0WlAy":{"description":"<p>The beyond terror's entrance into reality negates gravity in a localized area, resembling the zero-g vacuum of space.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 13 Arcana or DC 13 Occultism (trained) to temporarily counter the hazard's gravitational influence, preventing it from changing the gravity level on its next turn. The hazard is permanently disabled when the beyond terror is defeated.</p>","reset":"<p>The hazard doesn't reset once the beyond terror is defeated.</p>","routine":"<p>(1 action) On each of the hazard's turns, gravity in its affected area (indicated by a dotted line on the map) alters by one step, going from normal to low on turn 1 and low to zero on turn 2. From turn 3 onward, the area shifts between zero and low gravity on each alternating turn, and continues to do so until the hazard is disabled.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Losing Gravity","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The beyond terror appears</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The ground shakes and small pieces of rock and crystal levitate into the air. The hazard rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/FG5LKENqeKaVqCMn":{"lang":["Akitonian","Common","Shobhad"],"lore":[["Shobhad Lore",4]],"gear":["Shobhad Longrifle","Microcord Armor","Silencer (Commercial)","Sniper's Scope (Commercial)","Projectile Ammo (20)"],"focus":1,"abilities":[{"n":"World-Blessed Tracker","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>While she's on Akiton, Aruk automatically succeeds at Survival checks to Track made during exploration mode.</p>"},{"n":"Vitality Network","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Aruk has a vitality network they share with up to 10 bonded allies. This network can store a maximum of 14 healing Hit Points, begins combat full, and regains 4 healing Hit Points per round.</p>"},{"n":"Transfer Vitality","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","healing"],"f":"","d":"<p>Aruk transfers up to 10 healing Hit Points from her vitality network to a bonded creature she can sense within 60 feet. This works on creatures with void healing as though this action had the void trait.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/vRPjDT1NWrzZ53rl":{"lang":["Akitonian","Common"],"gear":["Degradation Grenade (Commercial) (2)","Hammer","Laser Rifle","Armored Coat","Medpatch (Commercial)","Battery (Commercial) (2)"]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/03CDlYI30GF5Pep1":{"abilities":[{"n":"Thoughtsense","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The beyond terror senses a creature's mental activity as a precise sense within the listed range; it cannot sense mindless creatures with thoughtsense.</p>"},{"n":"Horrors Beyond","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Creatures Swallowed Whole by the beyond terror are subjected to the constant mental assault of an entire world's collective, crushing existential fear. They have 2 fewer rounds before they begin suffocating, and after their escape, they are Stunned 1 for 1 round as their mind struggles to readjust after the ordeal.</p>"},{"n":"Inconceivable Feelings","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>As an entity of pure fear, the beyond terror cannot comprehend emotions outside its sphere of influence. When attempting Will saves against spells or effects with the emotion trait that deal with any emotion other than fear, the beyond terror treats its saving throw result as one step worse than what it rolls.</p>"},{"n":"Psychic Scream","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","emotion","fear","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>The beyond terror releases a psychic scream of horror that rings through every conscious mind in a 30-foot emanation, dealing 3d6 mental damage. All thinking creatures within range must attempt a DC 15 Will save. The beyond terror cannot use Psychic Scream again for 1d4 rounds.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes half damage.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage and is Frightened 1.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes double damage and is Frightened 2.</p>"},{"n":"Swallow Whole","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["attack"],"f":"","d":"<p>Large, 1d6+4 bludgeoning, Rupture 8</p><hr><p><p>The monster attempts to swallow a creature of the listed size or smaller that it has grabbed or restrained in its jaws or mouth. If a swallowed creature is of the maximum size listed, the monster can't use Swallow Whole again. If the creature is smaller than the maximum, the monster can usually swallow more creatures; the GM determines the maximum. The monster attempts an Athletics vs. Reflex DC check opposed by the grabbed creature's Reflex DC. If it succeeds, it swallows the creature. The monster's mouth or jaws no longer grab a creature it has swallowed, so the monster is free to use them to Strike or Grab once again. The monster can't attack creatures it has swallowed.</p>\n<p>A swallowed creature is Grabbed, is Slowed 1, and has to hold its breath or start suffocating. The swallowed creature takes the listed amount of damage when first swallowed and at the end of each of its turns while it's swallowed. If the victim Escapes this ability's grabbed condition, it exits through the monster's mouth. This frees any other creature grabbed in the monster's mouth or jaws. A swallowed creature can attack the monster that has swallowed it, but only with unarmed attacks or with weapons of light Bulk or less. The swallowing creature is Off-Guard against the attack. If the monster takes piercing or slashing damage equaling or exceeding the listed Rupture value from a single attack or spell, the swallowed creature cuts itself free. A creature that gets free by either Escaping or cutting itself free can immediately breathe and exits the swallowing monster's space.</p>\n<p>Effect: Engulf and Swallow Whole</p>\n<p>If the monster dies, a swallowed creature can be freed by creatures adjacent to the corpse if they spend a combined total of 3 actions cutting the monster open with a weapon or unarmed attack that deals piercing or slashing damage.</p></p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/BG73XJoTgKsaYSle":{"lang":["Akitonian","Common","Shobhad"],"gear":["Hardlight Handwraps (Advanced)","Painglaive","Grenade Launcher (Tactical)","Frag Grenade (Advanced) (6)","Armored Coat","Battery (Commercial)"],"abilities":[{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Rallied by the Beasts","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"once per day","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p>\n<p><strong>Requirements</strong> Bo-Shek has 35 Hit Points or less</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Bo-Shek howls a defiant roar and the Beasts of Bo respond in kind. He gains 10 temporary Hit Points that last 1 minute. As long as he has temporary Hit Points remaining, he deals an additional 1d6 precision damage with his melee Strikes.</p>"},{"n":"Supercharged Swing","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If Bo-Shek dealt damage to a creature with his painglaive while it was boosted, he additionally knocks the target back 10 feet, or 20 feet on a critical hit.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/2cZl1pGvCkPwprP2":{"description":"<p>The bumpers on the bridge push forward, attempting to knock competitors into the river.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 16 Thievery (trained) to shut off the mechanisms</p>","routine":"<p>(3 actions) The bumper bridge attempts to Shove all creatures on the bridge into the river with an Athletics bonus of +9 (no multiple attack penalty).</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(trained)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Into the Drink!","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature ends its movement on the bridge</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The bumper bridge attempts to Shove that creature into the river with an Athletics bonus of +9. If the triggering creature was not aware of this hazard, they take a –2 circumstance penalty to their Fortitude DC. The bumper bridge then rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/wOfIPn7lK7Cv641K":{"lang":["Common","Vlaka"],"gear":["Baton","Pulsecaster Pistol","Armored Coat","Battery (Commercial) (2)","Silver Pieces (10)"],"abilities":[{"n":"Nihilistic Pronouncement","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A Burnt Circle conspirator spouts some of their nihilistic teachings to a creature within 30 feet. They attempt a Demoralize check using Occultism in place of Intimidation.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/KJU9yXcN1C3C2YXY":{"abilities":[{"n":"Armored Deflection","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The cephalaspis corpse is the target of a physical ranged attack</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The cephalaspis corpse deflects the attack with the armored plates covering its head, gaining a +2 circumstance bonus to AC against the triggering attack.</p>"},{"n":"Cephalaspis Charge","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The cephalaspis corpse Strides twice, then makes an armored crest Strike. A Medium or smaller creature struck by this attack must succeed at a DC 15 Reflex save or be automatically Shoved back 5 feet and knocked Prone by the force of the blow.</p>"},{"n":"Pummeling Loop","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["move"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The cephalaspis corpse has a Medium or smaller creature Grabbed</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The cephalaspis corpse attempts an Athletics check to Reposition the grabbed creature, with the following results.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The cephalaspis corpse Flies 30 feet straight up and then drops the creature, causing it to fall.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> As critical success, but only 20 feet.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> No effect.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is no longer grabbed.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/qfdfi0hQZNxKgomJ":{"lang":["Akitonian","Common","Kasatha","Shobhad"],"gear":["Laser Pistol","Microcord Armor","Battery (Commercial) (2)"],"abilities":[{"n":"Reach Spell","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","spellshape"],"f":"","d":"<p>Chendre can extend the range of her spells. If the next action she uses is to Cast a Spell that has a range, increase that spell's range by 30 feet.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/ayOJu6R5zjVxiVkw":{"abilities":[{"n":"Gnaw Scrap","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["exploration"],"f":"","d":"<p>A khefak chews on an unattended object to feed, dealing 4 piercing damage every 10 minutes to the object. This damage ignores 10 points of Hardness. If a khefak doesn't spend at least 1 hour Gnawing Scrap per day, it begins to starve until it spends 10 minutes Gnawing Scrap.</p>"},{"n":"Nanite Repair","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"once per day","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Nanites implanted in the converted khefak's body repair its wounds, restoring 2d6 healing Hit Points.</p>"},{"n":"Trenching Teeth","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The converted khefak hit with a mandible Strike on its most recent action this turn</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The converted khefak quickly rotates the jagged serrations along its mandibles, dealing 1d10 slashing damage to the creature it hit with its mandible Strike.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/f1ikMjMJYAb2Mk6M":{"lang":["Akitonian","Common"],"gear":["Arc Pistol","Tempweave","Battery (Commercial)"],"abilities":[{"n":"Enhance Mutation","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["manipulate"],"f":"","d":"<p>The converted local taps into magic of their mutation, amplifying their power. Their monstrous claw Strikes deal an additional 1d6 acid damage until the start of their next turn.</p>"},{"n":"Supernatural Dash","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The converted local rushes forward at supernatural speed. They Stride twice.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/gwNMKzzWaFL8knTn":{"notes":{"per":"darkvision, snow vision"},"flavor":"<p>Yearling arabuks collect in glarings. They're abandoned by their mothers days after birth, then adopted by a mature arabuk that raises them as a group.</p><hr><p>Those traveling through Akiton's Winterlands risk stumbling on its apex predator: the carnivorous arabuk.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Snow Vision","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Snow doesn't impair a yearling arabuk's vision; it ignores Concealment from snowfall.</p>"},{"n":"Glacial Stride","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The arabuk Strides twice with a +10-foot circumstance bonus to Speed, ignoring difficult terrain caused by ice, snow, or other arctic conditions.</p>"},{"n":"Harmonic Hum","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","sonic"],"f":"","d":"<p>The arabuk's antlers reverberate a discordant anthem, dealing 2d4 sonic damage to all non-arabuk creatures in a 15-foot emanation. Any other arabuks within 60 feet can shake their antlers to add their harmonics to this chorus as a reaction. For each arabuk that does, the area of Harmonic Hum increases by 15 feet, to a maximum of a 60-foot emanation.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/LrUufeCKPWfiIlB5":{"abilities":[{"n":"Burst Pustule","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The gliding bear is dealt damage</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> One of the gliding bear's pustules pops, spraying putrid fluid in a 5-foot emanation. All creatures in the area become Sickened 1 unless they succeed at a DC 15 basic Fortitude save.</p>"},{"n":"Mauling Rush","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The gliding bear Strides up to double its Speed in a straight line, Climbing and Leaping over any obstacles in its way. At the end of this movement, it can attempt a melee Strike. On a hit, it additionally knocks the target Prone.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/T64s65XbZIdo5SJp":{"abilities":[{"n":"Ferocity","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster is reduced to 0 HP.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster avoids being knocked out and remains at 1 HP, but its Wounded value increases by 1. When it is Wounded 3, it can no longer use this ability</p></p>"},{"n":"Boar Charge","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The cy-boar Strides twice and then makes a tusk Strike. As long as it moved at least 20 feet, it gains a +2 circumstance bonus to its attack roll.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/46JDWaJs5nhrQHuO":{"abilities":[{"n":"Bursting Rubble","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The drillworm burrows up to its Speed and then emerges onto the surface. All creatures adjacent to it when it ends its movement must succeed at a DC 13 Reflex save or be knocked Prone.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/uDXp1amRSKObcGj1":{"lang":["Common"],"lore":[["Hellknight Lore",3]],"gear":["Knife","Laser Rifle","Skyfire Armor","Battery (Commercial) (2)"]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/RGpcMznWR60wmvxU":{"description":"<p>A makeshift catapult launches a dozen twi-lw fruits at all creatures in a wide area when a creature enters a selected 5-foot square.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 14 Survival or DC 14 Thievery to disable the triggering pressure plate.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Bombs Away!","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature enters the designated square</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The catapult launches a dozen twi-lw fruits through the air, dealing 2d4 bludgeoning damage to the triggering creature and all creatures in a 5-foot emanation centered on the triggering creature. Targeted creatures can attempt a DC 16 basic Reflex save. A creature that fails their save is additionally coated in sticky fruit, becoming Clumsy 1 for 1d4 rounds (1 minute on a critical failure).</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/micllXbcz1eBcAoz":{"lang":["Pyric"],"lore":[["Plane of Fire Lore",4]],"notes":{"per":"smoke vision"},"flavor":"<p>Fire wisps are sizzling spheres of flame and ash, perpetually crackling and shimmering with heat. They're carefree, boisterous, and quick to action—sometimes recklessly so.</p><hr><p>Wisps are tiny elemental beings that emerged during the creation of the Elemental Planes. The first wisps roamed the Inner Sphere in shifting symphonies that traded members with their every meeting. These symphonies of free wisps created music out of their combined resonances, but when the wicked Elemental Lords realized the value of the wisps' resonance, they captured whole symphonies for use as servants.</p>\n<p>Wisps attune to each other and to those they surround themselves with. This attunement makes them naturally supportive allies. Free wisps still roam the Inner Sphere and the Universe, but they're usually shy and hide themselves from strangers. However, they happily offer their service to those who show them kindness. They especially find themselves drawn to spellcasters who practice elemental magic; these wisps usually watch from afar but sometimes approach those who seem safe to become familiars or comrades.</p>\n<p>Free wisps who find one another become close almost immediately. They get especially excited when they find wisps of elements other than their own, showing none of the animosity sometimes exhibited between elementals of different planes. Instead, they join in an excited dance, emitting resonances that faintly echo the symphonies of ancient days.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Smoke Vision","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The fire wisp ignores the Concealed condition from smoke.</p>"},{"n":"Accord Essence","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["fire"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An ally within 30 feet that benefited from the wisp's resonance in the last hour is targeted by an attack</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The wisp detonates themself in an elemental explosion. This grants temporary Hit Points equal to half the wisp's current Hit Points to allies within 30 feet who have benefited from the wisp's resonance in the last hour. These temporary Hit Points last 1 hour.</p>\n<p>A wisp that uses this reaction is permanently destroyed, and they can be restored by only a Wish ritual or similarly powerful effect. If an ability would prevent the wisp's destruction (for instance, if the wisp is summoned and would merely be dismissed), Accord Essence has no effect.</p>"},{"n":"Resonance","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","fire"],"f":"","d":"<p>30 feet. All wisps vibrate at a frequency attuned to their element, resonating with and empowering all creatures and effects sharing that trait.</p>\n<p>A creature in the area gains a +1 status bonus to attack and damage rolls for effects with the fire trait; a creature with the elemental and fire traits gains this bonus to all attack and damage rolls.</p>"},{"n":"In Concert","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When a fire wisp rolls a critical failure on a check to Aid, they get a failure instead, and when they roll a success, they get a critical success instead.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/AbnUJaMIAK3l3mgN":{"lang":["Common","Draconic","Triaxian"],"gear":["Baton","Zero Pistol","Armored Coat","Medpatch (Commercial) (2)","Spell Gem of Thunderstrike (Rank 1)","Chem Tank (Commercial)"]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/JvX6eYrXNanEGLUm":{"lang":["Common","Draconic","Triaxian"],"gear":["Laser Rifle","Shotalashu Armor","Medpatch (Commercial)","Battery (Commercial)"],"abilities":[{"n":"Dragonkin Breath","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["fire"],"f":"","d":"<p>The dragonkin exhales a 15-foot cone of fire that deals 2d4 fire damage (DC 13 basic Reflex save). They can't use Dragonkin Breath again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/pqixotYFPLMMmEnU":{"gear":["Incendiary Grenade (Commercial) (2)","Pulsecaster Pistol","Singing Spear","Armored Coat","Battery (Commercial) (2)"]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/cHhQgQTfJvwdJtBV":{"notes":{"per":"electrolocation (precise) 30 feet"},"abilities":[{"n":"Electrolocation","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The creature can sense the electric field given off by living creatures, allowing them to precisely target living creatures without using visual means.</p>"},{"n":"Constrict","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>1d4+3 bludgeoning, DC 15 basic Fortitude</p><hr><p><p>The monster deals the listed amount of damage to any number of creatures Grabbed or Restrained by it. Each of those creatures can attempt a basic Fortitude save with the listed DC.</p></p>"},{"n":"Grasping Leap","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The girendal Leaps up to its Speed, and then makes an Athletics check to Grapple a target within reach of its tentacles. On a critical success the target is additionally knocked Prone.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/P7sZxfsmVhDWjvLY":{"lang":["Akitonian","Common","Necril","Primacy","Trinary","Vesk","Ysoki"],"lore":[["Engineering Lore",16]],"notes":{"hp":"void healing"},"abilities":[{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Constrict","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>2d10+4 bludgeoning, DC 25 basic Fortitude</p><hr><p><p>The monster deals the listed amount of damage to any number of creatures Grabbed or Restrained by it. Each of those creatures can attempt a basic Fortitude save with the listed DC.</p></p>"},{"n":"Manifold Hold","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Gremmik Integrated can have up to 4 creatures Grabbed at the same time, each with a different leg.</p>"},{"n":"Neural Integration","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Gremmik Integrated can communicate wirelessly with Elovai while within the <em>Wreck of the Returned</em>.</p>"},{"n":"Too Many Legs!","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Gremmik Integrated makes a leg Strike against each enemy within reach, up to a maximum of eight targets. He takes a –2 circumstance penalty on these attacks, but his multiple attack penalty doesn't increase until after these attacks are complete. He can't Grab with any leg Strikes made this way.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/6C2gf4u5PhsYb7LL":{"description":"<p>Gremmik Integrated blasts the four 10-foot square grates with steam from underneath, using the water that cools the servers.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 18 Crafting or DC 18 Engineering lore to cover the vents or DC 20 Thievery to Disable the mechanics; four total successes are required as each grate must be disabled. Once a grate is disabled, it no longer deals damage.</p>","routine":"<p>All creatures in or above the four 10-foot square vents are dealt 4d4 fire damage (DC 20 basic Reflex save)</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(trained)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Heat Up!","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Gremmik Integrated rolls initiative</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The vents heat up, releasing a puff of steam from each of the four 10-foot square vents. The trap then rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/FP7Al575O1l4n8Fw":{"description":"<p>Gremmik Integrated uses the holographic display from the center platform to distract and confuse one PC</p>","disable":"<p>DC 18 Computers to reprogram the display or DC 20 Thievery to turn it off entirely; three total successes are required.</p>","routine":"<p>The holographic display targets one creature within 20 feet of the platform, quickly displaying and changing graphs, logos, and videos. The creature must attempt a DC 20 Will save, with the following results.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected by the holographic display and is immune to its effects.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is unaffected by the holographic display.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is distracted by the holographic display and is Off-Guard for one round.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is fully invested in the information being displayed and is off-guard and Dazzled for one round.</p><hr><p>Note: A DC for this ability was not provided by Paizo. A value of 20 has been used following the hazard building rules.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(trained)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Flicker and Flash","a":"1","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Gremmik Integrated rolls initiative</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The holograms flicker wildly and increase in brightness. The trap then rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/EqQuzg5CEWRDekrj":{"abilities":[{"n":"Attach","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When the ichor mite bites a creature larger than itself, its mouth parts attach it to that creature. This is similar to Grabbing the creature, but the ichor mite moves with the creature rather than holding it in place. The ichor mite is Off-Guard while attached.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/0ODr0WRuhSB5kxpz":{"lang":["Aklo","Common","Telepathy 60 feet"],"abilities":[{"n":"Hallucinate","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>An Ichorwell handler's stomach fluids are laced with hallucinogens. A creature hit with projectile vomit must succeed at a DC 13 Will save or be Confused for 1 round.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/AFAUivepT8nW1efj":{"lang":["Aklo","Common","Telepathy 60 feet"],"gear":["Freebooter Armor"],"abilities":[{"n":"Siphon Blood","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["flourish"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The Ichorwell raider has a creature Grabbed</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The raider uses its proboscis to drink the blood of the grabbed creature, dealing 1d4 untyped damage. A creature that has its blood drained by a raider is Drained 1 until it receives healing of any kind or amount.</p>"},{"n":"Spew Vomit","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["acid"],"f":"","d":"<p>The Ichorwell raider spews vomit in a 15-foot cone, dealing 2d6 acid damage (DC 16 basic Fortitude save). The Ichorwell raider can't Spew Vomit again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/BepIu97cood0onql":{"lang":["Akitonian","Draconic","Shobhad"],"notes":{"per":"whispers of Akiton (imprecise) 60 feet"},"abilities":[{"n":"Whispers of Akiton","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Itaka can sense living creatures, objects and effects with the primal trait, and any objects and creatures in the area of primal effects, within range. She can also speak through primal effects, bypassing her selective silence.</p>"},{"n":"Selective Silence","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>5 feet. Itaka, willing creatures in the area, and creatures Grabbed or Restrained by Itaka or an affected ally make no sound (preventing speech and auditory actions).</p>"},{"n":"Suctioning Vortex","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["attack"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> Itaka doesn't have a creature Grabbed in its jaws</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Itaka draws breath into its powerful lungs to drag prey into its maw. Each creature in a 15-foot cone must succeed at a DC 18 Fortitude save or be pulled up to 10 feet closer to Itaka. Creatures that fail take 1d12 bludgeoning damage from the sudden pressure change. If at least one creature ends this forced movement adjacent to Itaka, Itaka can make a jaws Strike against that creature. If this Strike is a critical success, the creature is also grabbed in Itaka's jaws.</p>"},{"n":"Swallow Whole","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["attack"],"f":"","d":"<p>Medium, 2d4+2 cold, Rupture 7</p><hr><p><p>The monster attempts to swallow a creature of the listed size or smaller that it has grabbed or restrained in its jaws or mouth. If a swallowed creature is of the maximum size listed, the monster can't use Swallow Whole again. If the creature is smaller than the maximum, the monster can usually swallow more creatures; the GM determines the maximum. The monster attempts an Athletics vs. Reflex DC check opposed by the grabbed creature's Reflex DC. If it succeeds, it swallows the creature. The monster's mouth or jaws no longer grab a creature it has swallowed, so the monster is free to use them to Strike or Grab once again. The monster can't attack creatures it has swallowed.</p>\n<p>A swallowed creature is Grabbed, is Slowed 1, and has to hold its breath or start suffocating. The swallowed creature takes the listed amount of damage when first swallowed and at the end of each of its turns while it's swallowed. If the victim Escapes this ability's grabbed condition, it exits through the monster's mouth. This frees any other creature grabbed in the monster's mouth or jaws. A swallowed creature can attack the monster that has swallowed it, but only with unarmed attacks or with weapons of light Bulk or less. The swallowing creature is Off-Guard against the attack. If the monster takes piercing or slashing damage equaling or exceeding the listed Rupture value from a single attack or spell, the swallowed creature cuts itself free. A creature that gets free by either Escaping or cutting itself free can immediately breathe and exits the swallowing monster's space.</p>\n<p>Effect: Engulf and Swallow Whole</p>\n<p>If the monster dies, a swallowed creature can be freed by creatures adjacent to the corpse if they spend a combined total of 3 actions cutting the monster open with a weapon or unarmed attack that deals piercing or slashing damage.</p></p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/vs2a0zM7cH4sdsii":{"notes":{"hp":"void healing"},"abilities":[{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Corpse Chorus","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["fear","mental","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p>The jellied rat king loosens its ooze-like flesh, allowing the tiny rat corpses inside of it to open their mouths and wail horrifically. All creatures within 30 feet must succeed on a DC 15 Will save or become Frightened 1 (Frightened 2 on a critical failure).</p>"},{"n":"Dance of the Jellied Rats","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The jellied rat king spins and swirls, letting the tiny rat corpses inside of it bulge out inside its body like bludgeons. It deals 2d6 bludgeoning damage to all creatures in a 10-foot emanation (DC 15 basic Reflex save).</p>"},{"n":"Primordial Plague","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["poison"],"f":"","d":"<p>A living creature struck by a jellied rat king's jaws must attempt a DC 15 Fortitude save. On a failure, the creature becomes Sickened 1. If the creature is already sickened, the value of their sickened condition increases by 1, to a maximum of Sickened 2. When a creature succeeds at its saving throw, it is temporarily immune to primordial plague for 24 hours.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/xGJ40wADwMzAnZu0":{"description":"<p>A haphazardly constructed slug thrower with a barrel of discarded munitions, nails, and shrapnel has an advanced laser targeting system to identify and attack enemies.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 17 Computers (trained) to override the targeting system's friend/foe profiles, DC 15 Crafting (trained) to cut the turret's power, or DC 17 Thievery (trained) to disable the turret.</p>","reset":"<p>The trap resets after 1 minute.</p>","routine":"<p>(2 actions) The turret makes a junkslug Strike against up to two creatures in range, or multiple Strikes against a single creature in range if it has no additional targets.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(trained)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Junk Volley","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An enemy creature moves within 30 feet of the turret</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The turret makes a junkslug Strike against the triggering creature, then rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/oyVJBe3Y0O8DDbxX":{"abilities":[{"n":"Arctic Adaptation","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The kaylix treats environmental cold effects as if they were two steps less severe, and it isn't impeded by difficult terrain caused by snow, permafrost, ice, or other arctic terrain.</p>"},{"n":"Defensive Fling","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The kaylix has a creature Grabbed</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature other than the one the kaylix has grabbed makes a melee or ranged attack against the kaylix from within the range of the kaylix's quill Strike</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The kaylix makes a quill Strike against the attacking creature. This Strike doesn't count toward the kaylix's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p>"},{"n":"Concealing Condensation","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The kaylix opens gill-like vents on the side of its neck and releases hot, moist air that forms a concealing cloud of white mist in a 20-foot emanation centered on its location. This mist lingers until the end of the kaylix's next turn. All creatures within the mist become Concealed, and all creatures outside the mist become concealed to creatures within it.</p>"},{"n":"Pounce","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The kaylix Strides and makes a Strike at the end of that movement. If the kaylix began this action Hidden, it remains hidden until after the attack.</p>"},{"n":"Sneak Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The kaylix deals 1d6 extra precision damage to Off-Guard creatures.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/mIHt20etMrH2hPqJ":{"lang":["Akitonian","Common","Trinary","Vesk","Ysoki"],"gear":["Arc Rifle","Cryopike","Frag Grenade (Advanced) (4)","Second Skin","Functionary's Mask","Battery (Advanced)","Battery (Commercial)"],"abilities":[{"n":"Networked","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The Functionary can communicate wirelessly with converted locals and nodocites within 200 feet.</p>"},{"n":"Insult to Injury","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An enemy creature within 30 feet is damaged by a Strike</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The Functionary attempts to Demoralize the triggering creature.</p>"},{"n":"Command the Converted","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The Functionary successfully Strikes a target or a target fails their save against the Functionary's Area Fire</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The Functionary commands one of their allies to press the attack; that ally can use a reaction to make a Strike against the same target.</p>"},{"n":"Unreadable Aim","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The Functionary Feints against an opponent at a range of 100 feet. If she succeeds, the opponent is Off-Guard against her melee and ranged attacks, rather than only her melee attacks.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/SM8LX6gYc0S0uVnV":{"lang":["Common","Shobhad","Fey"],"gear":["Shobhad Longrifle","Projectile Ammo (8)"],"abilities":[{"n":"Reverberant Antlers","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["primal","sonic"],"f":"","d":"<p>Magical vibrations resonate through Kuriaku from his antlers. A creature that starts its turn Grabbed or Restrained by Kuriaku must succeed at a DC 14 Fortitude save or be Clumsy 1 and Stupefied 1 for 1 round (1 hour on a critical failure). A restrained creature uses the outcome one degree of success worse than its result.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"},{"n":"Knockdown","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Knockdown in its damage entry</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts to Trip the creature. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the monster's multiple attack penalty.</p></p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/yk8v4gI1QCRHYPls":{"description":"<p>A simple landmine buried in the ground explodes when pressure is applied.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 12 Crafting, DC 12 Survival, or DC 12 Thievery to carefully deactivate the mine's trigger</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Explode","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> a creature enters the landmine's area</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The landmine explodes, dealing 1d4 piercing damage to all creatures in a 5-foot emanation (DC 16 basic Reflex save)</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/JGivCIgqXMqhmoHF":{"description":"<p>A ceiling mounted turret fires a laser when intruders approach area <strong>B13</strong>.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 18 Computers (trained) to reprogram the turret, or DC 17 Crafting (trained) to cut power to the turret, or DC 16 Thievery (trained) to disable the turret</p>","routine":"<p>(3 actions) The trap makes three laser Strikes, each targeting a different creature unless there are fewer than three creatures in range.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(trained)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Laser Blast","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature moves within 30 feet of the turret</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The trap makes a laser Strike against the creature. The trap then rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/WHHTO9dJXN3XQCQp":{"description":"<p>A levitating cube that hums with power fires corrosive beams at intruders.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 18 Arcana or DC 18 Occultism (trained) to disrupt the device's magical currents, DC 19 Computers (trained) to reprogram the device, or DC 17 Thievery (trained) to disable the turret</p>","routine":"<p>(3 actions) The trap makes a degradation beam Strike against up to three creatures in range or three Strikes against one creature in range if it has no additional targets.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(trained)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Unmake Intruder","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature moves within 30 feet of the device</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The trap makes a degradation beam Strike against the creature; the trap then rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/UZkkTncVBSPb1SHn":{"lang":["Common"],"lore":[["Newborn Lore",5]],"gear":["Aucturnite Chakram","Laser Pistol","Battery (Commercial) (2)"]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/ilRv1Lty4l6vcFEJ":{"abilities":[{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Conversion Infection","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["disease","mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 20 Fortitude,</p>\n<p><strong>Onset</strong> 1 round,</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 1</strong> Stupefied 1 (1 day),</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 2</strong> Drained 1 and stupefied 1 (1 day),</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 3</strong> Drained 2 and Stupefied 2,</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 4</strong> mind-controlled minion of Elovai plus unique mutation</p>"},{"n":"Inject Conversion","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The nodocite assimilator makes an injector Strike. On a success, the target is also infected with conversion—an incredibly painful magical transformation the that mutates the target and turns them into a mind-controlled minion of Elovai.</p>"},{"n":"Networked Nodocite","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A nodocite can communicate wirelessly with other nodocites within 200 feet.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/TUDnG2r3f2YDF0Jx":{"notes":{"speed":"hover"},"abilities":[{"n":"Networked Nodocite","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A nodocite can communicate wirelessly with other nodocites within 200 feet.</p>"},{"n":"Spinning Deflection","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The nodocite blaster is the target of a physical attack they're aware of</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The nodocite blaster spins rapidly, becoming a blur of motion and gaining a +2 circumstance bonus to AC against the triggering attack.</p>"},{"n":"Lightning Spray","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The nodocite blaster sprays electric sparks in a 15-foot cone, dealing 3d6 electricity damage (DC 21 basic Reflex save).</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/bYzdDu0dcWV6wMyQ":{"abilities":[{"n":"Networked Nodocite","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A nodocite can communicate wirelessly with other nodocites within 200 feet.</p>"},{"n":"Dizzying Anesthetic","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["poison"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 13 Fortitude</p>\n<p><strong>Maximum Duration</strong> 6 rounds</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 1</strong> 1 poison damage and Clumsy 1 (1 round)</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 2</strong> 1d4 poison damage and clumsy 1 (1 round)</p>"},{"n":"Surgical Assault","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The nodocite experimenter attacks all creatures adjacent to it with its scalpels in a rapid and wild assault, dealing 1d4 slashing damage to all creatures within reach (DC 13 basic Reflex save).</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/ZsuOvgpjK3QnY076":{"gear":["Integrated Tactical Reality Ripper","Battery (Commercial)"],"abilities":[{"n":"Networked Nodocite","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A nodocite can communicate wirelessly with other nodocites within 200 feet.</p>"},{"n":"Warpwave","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once every 10 minutes</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature targets the nodocite gunner with an attack</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The nodocite gunner warps reality around itself, gaining a +2 circumstance bonus to its AC against the triggering attack.</p>"},{"n":"Assess Target","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The nodocite gunner assesses a target within 200 feet and pinpoints gaps in their defenses. Until the end of the nodocite gunner's turn, they deal an additional 1d8 damage with their reality ripper against the Assessed Target and increase the range increment of their reality ripper to 80 feet.</p>"},{"n":"Reality Cage","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per hour</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The nodocite guardian bends reality to trap one Medium or smaller creature within 60 feet in a cage of warped reality. The target must attempt a DC 20 Reflex save.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target is unaffected, and the reality cage fails to form.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The target is hindered by reality shards, becoming Off-Guard for 1 round; the reality cage fails to form.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The target is trapped in a reality cage that lasts 1d4 rounds.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The target is trapped in a reality cage that lasts 1 minute. A reality cage has AC 10, Hardness 5, and 10 Hit Points (BT 5). A creature trapped in a reality cage is Immobilized (Escape DC 20). A reality cage provides lesser cover.</p>"}],"strikeNotes":{"Reality Ripper":"<p>modular [acid and razing or void and concussive]</p>"}},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/0oPB5kHsKxHhsb9b":{"abilities":[{"n":"Networked Nodocite","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A nodocite can communicate wirelessly with other nodocites within 200 feet.</p>"},{"n":"Lunging Bite","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The nodocite hunter Strides up to its Speed then makes a jaws Strike. If it moved at least 15 feet with Lunging Bite, the target is Off-Guard against this Strike.</p>"},{"n":"Target Lock","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The nodocite hunter's last action was a successful jaws Strike</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The nodocite hunter assesses the biometrics and genetic material of the creature it bit, storing this genetic material in an internal cavity and locking onto the associated target's DNA. The nodocite hunter gains a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks to Seek the target and Survival checks to Track the target for 24 hours or until the nodocite hunter locks onto another target, whichever is first.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/nsQIOoOpAbOLxhGl":{"abilities":[{"n":"Networked Nodocite","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A nodocite can communicate wirelessly with other nodocites within 200 feet.</p>"},{"n":"Catchapon","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> A Grabbed, Immobilized, Paralyzed, Restrained, or Unconscious creature is within 15 feet of the nodocite incarcerator</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The nodocite incarcerator attempts to inhale the required creature. The target must attempt a DC 18 Fortitude save. On a failure, they're pulled into a miniaturized pocket dimension in a clear polymer ball and stored in the nodocite incarcerator's dorsal chamber.</p>\n<p>Each polymer ball weighs light Bulk and contains an individual pocket dimension that can hold one creature of any size at a time. Creatures inside are held in stasis, immune to the effects of time and dying, and are unable to act until released. A nodocite incarcerator can store an unlimited number of polymer balls in its dorsal chamber. When a nodocite incarcerator is destroyed, it automatically Vends all the polymer balls in its dorsal chamber.</p>\n<p>A creature within reach of the nodocite incarcerator can attempt a Athletics check to Force Open or a Computers, Crafting, or Thievery check to Disable Device; on a success, rather than the usual effects, the nodocite incarcerator immediately Vends one polymer ball (or two polymer balls on a critical success). It Vends the most recently filled polymer ball.</p>\n<p>A creature holding a polymer ball can throw the polymer ball up to 20 feet away as a single action with the manipulate trait, releasing the contained creature into an adjacent space, restored to their normal size and in the state they were when they were captured in the polymer ball.</p>"},{"n":"Vend","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The nodocite incarcerator ejects the most recently filled polymer ball into an adjacent square.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/I6y9ktiUErMkTlVB":{"gear":["Incendiary Grenade (Commercial) (2)"],"abilities":[{"n":"Networked Nodocite","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A nodocite can communicate wirelessly with other nodocites within 200 feet.</p>"},{"n":"Block Path","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the nodocite's reach uses a move action or leaves a square during a move action it's using</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The nodocite sentry makes a melee Strike against the triggering creature. On a hit, the target's movement is additionally disrupted.</p>"},{"n":"Push","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Push in its damage entry</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts to Shove the creature. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the monster's multiple attack penalty. If Push lists a distance, change the distance the creature is pushed on a success to that distance.</p></p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/munaPpliuPalKWlz":{"abilities":[{"n":"Networked Nodocite","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A nodocite can communicate wirelessly with other nodocites within 200 feet.</p>"},{"n":"Reality Bubble","a":"r","c":"interaction","t":["magical","occult"],"f":"once per minute","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per minute</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature attempts to move within 30 feet of the nodocite surveiller</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The nodocite surveiller creates a bubble of disruptive magic, causing reality to ripple and warp around the triggering creature. The ground in a 10-foot burst around the triggering creature becomes difficult terrain.</p>"},{"n":"Record Video","a":"1","c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The nodocite surveiller records or stops recording its surroundings, automatically transmitting everything it records to the <em>Wreck of the Returned</em>. Destroying or removing a nodocite surveiller's recording capabilities requires a successful DC 14 Thievery check to Disable device.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/0U869OVc1YRUfjqB":{"lang":["Common","Pyric","Trinary"],"lore":[["Hellknight Lore",8]],"gear":["Semi-Auto Pistol","Plasma Sword","Incendiary Grenade (Commercial) (2)","Carbon Shield","Defiance Series","Projectile Ammo (10)","Battery (Commercial)"],"notes":{"ac":"(19 with shield raised)"},"abilities":[{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Shield Block","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster has its shield raised and takes damage from a physical attack.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster snaps its shield into place to deflect a blow. The shield prevents the monster from taking an amount of damage up to the shield's Hardness. The monster and the shield each take any remaining damage, possibly breaking or destroying the shield.</p></p>"},{"n":"Eclipse Beam","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p>Kanren channels destructive energy into his blade or shield then thrusts it forward, unleashing black hellfire in a 30-foot line. Creatures in the area are dealt 2d6 fire damage and can attempt a DC 15 basic Reflex save. On a critical failure, a creature is additionally Sickened 1.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/QkYQX3jAZJwFmWPc":{"abilities":[{"n":"Fireworks","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The plasma penguin is reduced to 0 Hit Points</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The plasma penguin explodes in a burst of fireworks, dealing 1d4 electricity plus 1d4 fire damage in a 5-foot emanation (DC 13 basic Reflex save).</p>"},{"n":"Plasma Slide","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["move"],"f":"","d":"<p>The plasma penguin Drops Prone, moves up to twice its Speed by sliding on its stomach, then Stands. It can then attempt a melee Strike against a creature within reach.</p>"},{"n":"Push","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Push in its damage entry</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts to Shove the creature. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the monster's multiple attack penalty. If Push lists a distance, change the distance the creature is pushed on a success to that distance.</p></p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/yyNlR5lslgPwqe78":{"description":"<p>The collective minds of Luvoth's sapient inhabitants lash out at the unknown in a storm of psychic confusion, fear, anger and pain.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 16 Arcana, DC 16 Nature, DC 16 Religion or DC 16 Occultism (trained) to soothe the restless emotions with prayer, meditative chanting, or magical rituals; three total checks are required to disable the hazard. The hazard is permanently disabled when the beyond terror is defeated.</p>","reset":"<p>The hazard remains active as long as the beyond terror is alive and doesn't reset once it's disabled or the beyond terror is defeated.</p>","routine":"<p>(1 action) On each of its turns, the hazard targets one of the PCs at random, dealing 2d4 mental damage with a DC 16 basic Will save. On a failure, the target also becomes Stupefied 1; on a critical failure, they become Stupefied 2.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Gathering Storm","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The beyond terror appears</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> A swirling green energy emerges from the world mirror, roiling through the air with a wail of confusion and fear. All creatures within 30 feet of the world mirror become Frightened 1 unless they succeed at a DC 16 Will save. The haunt then rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/KADM4F14urfQR9Cu":{"lang":["Akitonian","Common","Trinary","Ysoki","Primacy"],"gear":["Zero Pistol","Carbon Skin","Parallel Accord","Chem Tank (Commercial) (2)"],"notes":{"speed":"Hover"},"focus":1,"abilities":[{"n":"Quantum Pulse","a":"f","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Quantum Nexus rolls initiative</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Quantum Nexus releases a burst of energy and uses Warp Reality.</p>"},{"n":"Quantum Recycle","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"once per day","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Quantum Nexus casts a 2nd-rank spell, and the spell targets a creature or area within her quantum field</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Quantum Nexus manipulates her quantum field to preserve some spell energy and regains an expended 1st-rank spell slot.</p>"},{"n":"Harmonic Blink","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","teleportation"],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Quantum Nexus transports herself in the above of an eye, teleporting to a location up to 20 feet away within her line of sight.</p>"},{"n":"Warp Reality","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> Quantum Nexus's quantum field isn't active</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Quantum Nexus's quantum field activates and lasts as long as she Sustains it (up to 10 minutes) or until the end of her next turn. The quantum field is a 20-foot burst centered on a point she chooses within 100 feet. Whenever she Sustains it, she can Seek or Recall Knowledge against a target in the field as a free action. If she Sustained it with the Sustain action (instead of an anchoring action), she can move her quantum field to a new position within 100 feet. The field automatically deactivates if she's knocked out, if she Dismisses it, or if she moves more than 100 feet away from it.</p>"},{"n":"Witchwarper Paradox: Analyst","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/MJ4l0d89SqAfy1Tz":{"abilities":[{"n":"Flare Quills","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The quildebeest is hit with an unarmed Strike or a Strike with a non-reach melee weapon</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The quildebeest flares its crystalline quills, harming its attacker. The triggering creature is dealt 1d8 piercing damage (DC 18 basic Reflex save).</p>"},{"n":"Subsonic Harmonics","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","concentrate"],"f":"","d":"<p>The quildebeest unleashes a powerful sonic roar that deals 5d6 sonic damage in a 30-foot cone (DC 18 basic Fortitude save). On a critical failure, a creature is additionally Sickened 1, as the subsonic frequencies batter their internal organs. A quildebeest can't use Subsonic Harmonics again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/lj06NopCjL5TVgi3":{"description":"<p>A damaged device unleashes a blast of magical energy, which coalesces into a cyclone that degrades reality.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 17 Arcana or DC 17 Nature (trained) to diffuse magical energy, DC 18 Crafting or DC 18 Computers (trained) to shut down the device, DC 17 Occultism to stabilize reality, DC 18 Thievery (trained) to destabilize the cyclone, or Dispel Magic (2nd rank; counteract DC 16) to counteract the cyclone</p>","routine":"<p>(2 actions) The cyclone moves up to 30 feet toward the nearest living creature, then churns in place, degrading reality. All living creatures within 10 feet of the cyclone are dealt 1d8 acid damage, or 2d8 acid damage if the cyclone is in their space (DC 20 basic Reflex save).</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(trained) or Detect Magic</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Form Cyclone","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A living creature disturbs the debris in area <strong>A2</strong></p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> A cyclone of magical energy forms around the triggering creature, dealing 2d8 acid damage (DC 20 basic Reflex). This cyclone is 5-feet in diameter and 20-feet high. The trap then rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/4wblzSbaGKhezoer":{"description":"<p>Reality glitches, causing one of the camp's five areas to jump backward and forward in time, buildings and people alike dissolving in the temporal chaos.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 18 Arcana, DC 18 Nature, DC 18 Occultism, or DC 18 Religion (trained) to magically reinforce Akiton's reality, or DC 19 Intimidation (trained) to impose your will on the reality warp; must be in the hazard's active area to Disable it.</p>","routine":"<p>(2 actions) With its first action, reality warps in the hazard's active area, dealing 1d10+6 force damage to all creatures in that area (DC 20 basic Fortitude save). With its second action, the active hazard moves to a different area, determined randomly. Any creatures in this new active area must attempt a DC 20 Will save. On a failure, they are Stunned 1 as they try to process the changing reality; on a critical failure, they are also Off-Guard for 1 round.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Blip. Reset.","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature enters any area of the hazard</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The reality warp causes the timeline to repeatedly blip and reset, approximately every six seconds, causing the triggering creature to flicker back and forth in time. They must attempt a DC 20 Will save. The hazard rolls initiative and one area (<strong>A1</strong>–<strong>A5</strong>) becomes active, determined randomly.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The triggering creature uses the time blip to their advantage; on the first check they attempt on their turn each round, they can roll twice and take the better result, until the hazard is defeated. This is a fortune effect.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The triggering creature is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> On the first check the triggering creature attempts on their turn each round, they must roll twice and take the worse result, until the hazard is defeated. This is a misfortune effect.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, except the triggering creature must roll every check twice.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/wTNA31V4cZNUu78t":{"abilities":[{"n":"Gnaw Scrap","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["exploration"],"f":"","d":"<p>A khefak chews on an unattended object to feed, dealing 4 piercing damage every 10 minutes to the object. This damage ignores 10 points of Hardness. If a khefak doesn't spend at least 1 hour Gnawing Scrap per day, it begins to starve until it spends 10 minutes Gnawing Scrap.</p>"},{"n":"Tail Blast","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["acid","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The khefak flicks its tail, unleashing a blast of volatile magic that deals 3d6 acid damage in a 60-foot line (DC 18 basic Reflex save). It can't use Tail Blast again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/8awVBEcXh9GPsOtP":{"lang":["Akitonian","Common","Shobhad"],"gear":["Rotolaser","Freebooter Armor","Battery (Advanced) (2)"],"abilities":[{"n":"Defensive Shove","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An enemy ends a move action adjacent to Rip</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Rip attempts to Shove the triggering creature. If she would critically fail, she gets a failure instead.</p>"},{"n":"Pinpoint Fire","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Whenever Rip Auto-Fires her rotolaser, she excludes Tear from the area. Creatures that fail their save against her Auto-Fire are Suppressed until the beginning of her next turn.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/am2B0JJoDq9fqm2r":{"abilities":[{"n":"Motion Sense","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A robotic oil can feel nearby motion through vibration and air movement.</p>"},{"n":"Reparative Spray","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["magical"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per hour</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The robotic oil sprays fluids in a 10-foot emanation. All constructs in the area are repaired, regaining 1d6 healing Hit Points. All non-constructs in the area are dealt 2d6 acid damage with a DC 16 basic Reflex save.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/emME5GIloutQ1UX7":{"description":"<p>A hacking probe with built-in anti-tampering countermeasures.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 16 Thievery (trained) to disable the anti-intrusion sensor, DC 18 Computers (trained) or DC 18 Crafting (trained) to cut the power supply, or DC 20 Athletics to swiftly rip the power-pack out of the device before it can respond.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Blood Decayer","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":["void"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature fails to disable the device</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The trap releases a destabilizing bio-agent, dealing 6d6 void damage to all creatures within a 5-foot burst of the sequence breaker (DC 23 basic Fortitude save).</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/9Cm3LHfWDmMleLgn":{"description":"<p>The paintings weep blackness outward until they create shadows from floor to ceiling.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 20 Acrobatics (trained) to divert the energy of the spirits against each other, DC 18 Athletics (trained) to Grapple the spirits, or DC 18 Religion or DC 18 Occultism (trained) to soothe the restless souls; two successes are required to disable the hazard.</p>","reset":"<p>The haunt resets after 1 day.</p>","routine":"<p>(1 action) Shadowy hands lunge from the walls to drag down creatures in the room. The hazard attempts an Athletics check with a +12 modifier against the Fortitude DC of up to two different creatures in the room.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target takes 2d10+4 bludgeoning damage, is knocked Prone, and is pushed 10 feet toward the nearest wall. It can't breathe or speak until it ends the prone condition.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The target takes 1d10+4 bludgeoning damage and is pushed 5 feet toward the nearest wall.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(trained)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Cry of the Defeated","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["auditory","emotion","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A non-fey, non-shobhad creature passes the room's center</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The spirits howl in rage, dealing 2d4 mental damage to the triggering creature (DC 20 basic Will save). On a critical failure, that creature is also Deafened for 1 round. The hazard then rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/4miww4pZSgjTMMIw":{"lang":["Aklo","Common","Telepathy 60 feet"],"gear":["Reaction Breacher","Armored Coat","Projectile Ammo (15)"],"abilities":[{"n":"Psychic Resonance","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Shosodax has forged an intense psychic connection with their reaction breacher, channeling their hatred into every shot fired and wound inflicted. They deal an additional 1d8 mental damage with their reaction breacher (already included in damage) and their reaction breacher gains the magical trait.</p>"},{"n":"Raider's Assault","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Shosodax makes two ranged Strikes with their reaction breacher, each at a different target, then Interacts to reload their reaction breacher.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/GObiz79QPrANGm0a":{"description":"<p>A rapid sequence of dizzying simulations plays throughout the theater.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 17 Arcana, DC 17 Nature, DC 17 Occultism, or DC 17 Religion (trained) to siphon the magical energy, or DC 19 Thievery (trained) to disrupt the holograms, or Dispel Magic (2nd rank; counteract DC 16)</p>","routine":"<p>(1 action) The hazard plays a new simulation each round, forcing all creatures who can sense it to attempt a new save.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(trained) or Detect Magic</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Accelerated Simulation","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["incapacitation","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature enters the theater</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The trap launches a series of simulations at a dizzying pace, each slightly different from the previous one. All creatures in area <strong>B6</strong> who can see must attempt a DC 20 Will save. The trap the rolls initiative.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The target is Sickened 1 for 1 round.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The target takes 2d4 mental damage and is sickened 1.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The target takes 4d4 mental damage and is Sickened 2.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/mV3dWqSibGVyRwLu":{"abilities":[{"n":"T-Shirt Barrage","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The solar parade float shoots t-shirts at all enemies within 30 feet. Creatures in the area can attempt a DC 17 Reflex save. On a failure, the t-shirts wrap around their appendages, imposing a –10 foot circumstance penalty to all their Speeds until the end of their next turn. A creature can end this effect early as a single action with the manipulate trait.</p>"},{"n":"Trample","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Large or smaller, wheels, DC 17 basic Reflex. After using Trample, the solar parade float can't use Trample again for 2 rounds.</p><hr><p><p>The monster Strides up to double its Speed and can move through the spaces of creatures of the listed size, Trampling each creature whose space it enters. The monster can attempt to Trample the same creature only once in a single use of Trample. The monster deals the damage of the listed Strike, but trampled creatures can attempt a basic Reflex save at the listed DC (no damage on a critical success, half damage on a success, double damage on a critical failure).</p></p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/wRKjBpNeXzVvsjU8":{"description":"<p>Nozzles on the walls spray hot water, chemical sanitizers, and superheated air at all creatures entering the U-shaped hall.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 14 Computers (trained) to reprogram the system to safe levels, DC 14 Crafting (trained) to shut off the waterline, or DC 13 Thievery (trained) to cut power to the hall</p>","reset":"<p>The trap automatically deactivates and resets if there are no creatures in the area.</p>","routine":"<p>(2 actions) The trap sprays a powerful stream of superheated water and sanitizer at all creatures in the U-shaped hall, dealing 1d4 bludgeoning damage and 1d4 fire damage (DC 17 basic Reflex save).</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(trained)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Steam Clean","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["fire","water"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature ends its movement in the U-shaped hall</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The trap sprays a dense cloud of steam in the hall, obscuring vision. Creatures in the area are Concealed and creatures outside the hall are concealed to those within it. The trap then rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/JgNhb5TnOEFs6RKF":{"description":"<p>A log hung up in the trees swings down in a wide arc when a creature enters the designated 10-foot square area.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 14 Survival or DC 14 Thievery to safely sever the triggering pulleys and ropes.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Swing","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature enters the designated 10-foot square area</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The log swings along its course, making a log Strike against the triggering creature.</p>"}],"strikeNotes":{"Log":"<p>Plus knocked Prone</p>"}},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/kkHAbz2iZbL9nztb":{"lang":["Akitonian","Common","Primacy","Trinary","Ysoki"],"gear":["Laser Rifle","Semi-Auto Pistol (2)","Shock Pad","Second Skin","Battery (Tactical)","Projectile Ammo (40)","Battery (Commercial)"],"abilities":[{"n":"Networked","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Tade can communicate wirelessly with nodocites within 200 feet.</p>"},{"n":"Rapid Reconstruction","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Tade is dealt damage</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Magic surges through Tade's body, automatically reconstructing damaged flesh and muscle. Tade regains 5 healing Hit Points.</p>"},{"n":"Mass Reload","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Tade reloads up to two guns they're wielding.</p>"},{"n":"Multi-Weapon Aim","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> Tade is wielding at least one ranged weapon that doesn't have the area trait</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Tade takes careful aim at a single creature they're aware of, designating it as their mark. Until the end of Tade's turn, their ranged Strikes against their mark using any ranged weapon deal an additional 2d4 precision damage and reduce the circumstance bonus to AC their mark gains from cover by 1. Tade can only have one mark at a time.</p>"},{"n":"Relentless Fire","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Tade just keeps coming with their pistol fire. They make two ranged Strikes, one with each of their two semi-auto pistols. These strikes must be against different targets.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/hlGdpDtynomGpD4P":{"lang":["Akitonian","Common","Shobhad"],"gear":["Fangblade","Semi-Auto Pistol","Freebooter Armor","Battery (Tactical)","Projectile Ammo (10)"],"abilities":[{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Boosted Assault","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["move"],"f":"","d":"<p>Tear Leaps or Strides, then Interacts to boost her fangblade. If she ends her movement within reach of an enemy, she makes a fangblade Strike against that creature.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/CPscv2uLsixHSB3n":{"description":"<p>Metal caution-taped doors cover a 10-foot deep pit full of dull metal spikes.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 12 Thievery to lock or close the trap door</p>","reset":"<p>Creatures can still fall into the trap, but the trapdoor must be reset manually for the trap to become hidden again.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(or 0 if the trap door is open)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Pitfall","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature walks onto the trapdoor</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The triggering creature falls in and takes fall damage (typically 5; but 0 in Akiton's low gravity), plus an additional 2d4 piercing damage from the spikes (DC 16 basic Reflex save). The creature can use the Grab an edge reaction to avoid falling.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/8eymZB9KiXH3xfO0":{"abilities":[{"n":"Draw Power","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The unspooled vestige is hit by a ranged weapon that uses charges and has at least 1 charge remaining in its battery</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The unspooled vestige pulls energy from the weapon, causing it to expend an additional charge.</p>"},{"n":"Slip Out of Reality","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>At the end of its turn, the unspooled vestige must attempt a DC 11 Flat. On a failure, it slips slightly out of reality. It takes 1d4 force damage, and becomes Concealed until the start of its next turn.</p>"},{"n":"Entanglement","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A unspooled vestige filament becomes entangled with a creature it hits. The creature becomes Grabbed; they're not Immobilized, but they can't move beyond the range of the unspooled vestige's filament. The unspooled vestige can attempt to Reposition each entangled creature with a single Athletics check, which they compare against each creature's Fortitude DC. Doing so only counts as one attempt for the unspooled vestige's multiple attack penalty. The DC to Escape is 18, or a creature can sever the filament with a Strike against AC 15 that deals at least 3 slashing damage. This deals no damage to the unspooled vestige. The unspooled vestige can move without ending the entanglement as long as the creature remains within the filament's range.</p>"},{"n":"Unspool","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The fabric of the creature's reality begins to fray. The unspooled vestige must attempt a DC 16 Fortitude save. On a failure it takes 1d4 force damage, or 1d6 force damage on a critical failure.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/7pt4wcjtp4qfD7bm":{"description":"<p>The inflamed walls of this chamber violently contract, squirting out caustic fluids and pus.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 12 Medicine (trained) to ease the inflammation, or DC 13 Diplomacy or DC 13 Occultism (trained) to psychically soothe the structure; DC 16 Acrobatics or DC 16 Stealth to move through the area without triggering its spray (this doesn't disable the hazard).</p>","reset":"<p>The hazard resets after one hour.</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Spray Pus","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature enters one of the ichor-submerged spaces in this room</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The hazard sprays a stream of caustic fluids and pus at the triggering creature, dealing 2d6+3 acid damage (DC 16 basic Reflex save).</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/m4WJQtfujY5Q0vAE":{"lang":["Common","Eoxian","Necril"],"lore":[["Corpse Fleet Lore",14]],"gear":["Laser Pistol","Defiance Series","Spell Gem of Blazing Bolt (Rank 2)","Battery (Advanced) (2)"],"notes":{"hp":"void healing"},"abilities":[{"n":"Ulcerating Aura","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["arcane","aura","void"],"f":"","d":"<p>15 feet. A living creature entering or starting its turn in the aura must attempt a DC 19 Fortitude save as Vira's command over gravity causes their cells to expand rapidly. On a failure, their skin ruptures, dealing 1d6 persistent bleed damage. On a critical failure, they are also Stunned 1. A creature that succeeds on their saving throw is temporarily immune for 1 minute.</p>"},{"n":"Untethered Gravity","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>While Vira is in a vacuum or zero-g environment, she gains a fly Speed equal to her Speed.</p>"},{"n":"Thrashing Wisps","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature ends its movement adjacent to Vira</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Vira launches a wave of force at the triggering creature. The creature must succeed at a DC 19 Fortitude save or be pushed directly back 5 feet, or 10 feet on a critical failure. If the creature is in a vacuum or zero-g environment, they additionally become Untethered.</p>"},{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Gravitic Surge","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Vira's mastery of gravity allows her to augment the impact of her spells. If her next action is to cast a spell that deals damage while she's in a zero-g environment, the target takes an amount of persistent void damage equal to twice the spell's rank.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/LMI8A83YFnoSEKFn":{"notes":{"hp":"void healing"},"abilities":[{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Gorge","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The void hemovore's last action was a successful fangs Strike</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The void hemovore drinks the creature's blood. The creature must succeed at a DC 16 Fortitude save. On a failure, they become Drained 1, or they increase the value of their drained condition by 1, up to a maximum of Drained 2.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/MZuAysCxMqSQNZW9":{"description":"<p>An unnatural magical storm appears in the area with a crack of thunder and lightning.</p>","disable":"<p>DC 13 Arcana, DC 13 Nature, DC 13 Occultism, or DC 13 Religion (all trained) to overcome the magical anomaly, or DC 16 Athletics, DC 16 Survival, or DC 16 Thievery to destabilize the hazard's center point; two total successes are required to disable the hazard.</p>","routine":"<p>(3 actions) The hazard makes three ranged Strikes against PCs, selecting different targets if possible, beginning with those closest to the hazard's center.</p>","stealthNote":"<p>(trained)</p>","abilities":[{"n":"Electric Flash","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":["electricity"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A PC enters the area</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> With a flash of light, the area crackles with electricity, and it begins to rain. The triggering creature is dealt 1d6+2 electricity damage (DC 16 basic Reflex save). On a critical failure, that creature is additionally Dazzled for 1 round. The hazard then rolls initiative.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/NdqOLPOwZ1YweqII":{"lang":["Akitonian","Common","Trinary"],"gear":["Semi-Auto Pistol","Shock Pad","Hardlight Series","Hacking Toolkit (Commercial)","Infiltrator's Toolkit (Commercial)","Repair Toolkit (Commercial)","Machine Mind Serum (Commercial) (3)","Projectile Ammo (10)","Battery (Commercial)"],"notes":{"saves":"+1 vs disease, mental, poison, radiation"},"abilities":[{"n":"+1 to Saves Vs Disease, Mental, Poison, Radiation","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Nanite Surge","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"once per hour","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per hour</p>\n<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Whisper in the Code attempts a skill action that takes 3 or fewer actions</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Whisper in the Code stimulates their nanites, forcing their body to temporarily increase its efficiency. They gain a +2 status bonus to the triggering skill check. In addition, their circuitry glows, lighting a 10-foot emanation with dim light for 1 round.</p>"},{"n":"Reach Spell","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["spellshape"],"f":"","d":"<p>If the next action Whisper in the Code takes is to Cast a Spell that has a range, increase that spell's range by 30 feet.</p>"}]},"sf2e-anachronism.starfinder-society-bestiary/XytZxY2FixC9e5T9":{"lang":["Akitonian","Common","Shirren","Trinary"],"gear":["Plasma Caster","Tempweave","Battery (Tactical)"],"abilities":[{"n":"Amp the Voltage!","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["electricity","magical"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> Zizenzi's last action was a successful conductive spine Strike</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Zizenzi amps up the voltage in their conductive spines, causing immense pain to the injured target. The target must succeed at a DC 19 Fortitude save or become Sickened 1 from the pain (Sickened 2 on a critical failure).</p>"}]}});
